me-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "63"}, {"n": 19, "text": "The ratio of numbers of girls and boys participating in sports of a school is 1 : 5. If the number of girls is 239, determine the number of boys participating in the sports.", "options": [{"text": "1215", "added": false}, {"text": "1225", "added": false}, {"text": "1195", "added": false}, {"text": "1170", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "1195"}, {"n": 20, "text": "Find the simple interest (in closest integral ₹) on ₹3000 at 8% per annum rate of interest for the period from 23 February 2024 to 24 April 2024", "options": [{"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "40"}, {"n": 21, "text": "What happens when sodium hydroxide reacts with copper (II) sulfate solution?", "options": [{"text": "No reaction occurs.", "added": false}, {"text": "Sodium sulfate is formed.", "added": false}, {"text": "Copper metal is deposited.", "added": false}, {"text": "Copper(II) hydroxide precipitates.", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": "K=3; P=0"}, {"n": 22, "text": "A company earns a profit (in ₹) that is distributed among the company's three partners in the ratio of 4 : 12 : 5. If the difference between the smallest and the largest shares is ₹20208, the total profit (in ₹) of the company is:", "options": [{"text": "53097", "added": false}, {"text": "53060", "added": false}, {"text": "53046", "added": false}, {"text": "53096", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "53046"}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "49", "added": fals